   "text": {
    "L1": "Resources give us energy, materials, and water. We classify them by how quickly nature replaces them.",
    "L2": "Renewable resources are replaced in a short time, such as sunlight, wind, water, and replanted forests.",
    "L3": "Non-renewable resources are limited. Coal, petroleum, natural gas, and many minerals take millions of years to form.",
    "L4": "Here is a myth: renewable means unlimited. That is not true.",
    "L5": "Groundwater is renewable, but pumping it faster than rain refills it makes the level fall.",
    "L6": "Petrol is non-renewable, so using it wisely means sharing rides, using public transport, cycling, or choosing solar or electric where possible.",
    "L7": "We can also save water and reduce, reuse, and recycle. Now choose the renewable resource."
   },
